# 14z-107 (3) — tests/audit_sdram_bank_load.sh: the per-bank SDRAM traffic
# profile of stock vsavj on the STOCK cps2 core (2026-08-23).
# Fork pin 74ed17d (the fixed SDRAM model + the three `-stats` fixes).
# tests/replays/05_timeout_idle.rpl, 2800 ABSOLUTE frames, 63m36s wall.
#
# WHY: the maintainer ruled the MiSTer memory-map route is the BANK REPACK at
# our v1.7.3 pin — vanilla's 32 MB of GFX stays in banks 2+3 and the ~6.4 MB
# of tenant art goes into bank 1 beside the QSound PCM, reached by the
# profile-gated promoted tile-code bit — "attempt repack (measuring first)",
# with JTFRAME_SDRAM_XL as the fallback. This is the measuring.
#
# RE-DERIVE:  tests/audit_sdram_bank_load.sh --log <this file>
# The SDRAM_STATS_RAW series below is SAMPLED 1 IN 16 (352 of 5,620 lines) to
# keep the file at 68 kB; re-running the analysis on it reproduces every
# figure in the table to within 0.5%. No ROM bytes (CLAUDE.md rule 7).

